  "description": "An application submitted under Section 96a of the Town & Country Planning Act 1990 for a non-material amendment in connection with the planning permission (DC/17/103961) granted on the 20/12/2017  as amended by s.96a application DC/20/116104 approved on 15 April 2020 \"for demolition of Kenton Court, 132 Adamsrill Road SE26 and the construction of a part three/part four storey building to provide 25 residential dwellings comprised of 5 x 1 bed, 15 x 2 bed, 4 x 3 bed and 1 x 4 bed self contained flats, together with improvements to the existing pedestrian walkway, the creation of a shared landscaped space within a rear courtyard, secure cycle and refuse storage\" in order to:Alter unit mix to provide additional bedroomsAmend refuse and cycle store locationsSouth-east boundary treatments updatesreplacement of living wallUpdate entrance canopy details Internal communal and internal flat layout changes amend the wording of the description of development to reflect the revised unit mix to: \"demolition of Kenton Court, 132 Adamsrill Road SE26 and the construction of a part three/part four storey building to provide 25 residential dwellings, together with improvements to the existing pedestrian walkway, the creation of a shared landscaped space within a rear courtyard, secure cycle and refuse storage\"",
